  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;It&apos;s time for Gender Justice&quot; - Mainstreaming Gender into programmes</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To increase the conceptual understanding of gender and increase skills in gender analysis of staff in selected partners.
To increase skills for gender responsive programming, implementation and monitoring among project level staff in partner programmes.
To translate and apply CAFOD&apos;s gender policy into the working realities of different partners and programmes by developing gender mainstreaming tools and monitoring indicators.
To improve the capacity of CAFOD East Africa staff to follow up on gender mainstreaming processes among partners.
To make the gender analysis done by CAFOD more participatory and meaningful.
To promote ongoing dialogue on gender justice and the empowerment of women between CAFOD and its partners and develop a process for taking gender on board programmes.
To encourage gender sensitive policies and structures, such as gender working groups, in order to ensure self-motivated and self-sustaining gender responsive change within programmes.</narrative>
  </description>
